  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the triangles with vertices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the maximum and the minimum perimeters of such triangles are obtained at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></math> is equal to ___________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "48",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>The triangles with vertices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>And&nbsp;the maximum and the minimum perimeters of such triangles are obtained at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively,</p><p>Now to minimise <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></math>,&nbsp;in below diagram take image of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>,</p><p>We get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0050_91a789dcb9f2.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 188px;\" /></p><p>Now finding, equation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, putting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;in above equation we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, maximum&nbsp;perimeter&nbsp;will be possible if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Now taking&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Now when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Now on comparing the perimeter we get, maximum perimeter at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}